    "result_text": "The full suite (1 test) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. Since the build regenerates the DTO from `openapi.yml` and compiles the controller's `setBulkSignupWarning(...)` call, the new field is confirmed generated and wired.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` response flag for the PetClinic owner endpoints.\n\n**The rule:** when more than 80 owners have already been registered on the current business day, the owner response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` schema. Since DTOs are generated from this spec by the openapi-generator, this produces `OwnerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(...)`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant, alongside the existing per-city/per-day limit constants.\n   - Added a small private helper `toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning(Owner)` that maps the owner and stamps the flag based on `countOwnersRegisteredOn(today) > 80`, using `RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate(null)` for \"today\" (consistent with the existing daily-limit rule's date handling).\n   - Both `getOwner` and `addOwner` now use this helper, so the flag is present on create and read-back responses without duplicating logic.\n\n**Design notes:** The count query requires the `ClinicService`, which the pure MapStruct mapper doesn't have, so the flag is stamped in the controller where that collaborator already lives \u2014 matching the existing inline count-check idiom. The threshold and computation are isolated in one small, single-responsibility helper reused by both endpoints. Seed owners have `NULL` registration dates so they never count toward the day total, and the `@Transactional` acceptance test correctly sees `false` for a single fresh create.",
